build a more nuanced predictive model on what crowdfunding campaigns may succeed, and to what degree they will succeed. Since Kickstarter only makes money once a project has passed its goal \u2013 and has been deemed a success \u2013 it is already in their best interests to only have successful campaigns. But if there were a way to determine which campaigns would be extremely successful \u2013 and could theoretically be even more successful with the right publicity on their end \u2013 Kickstarter would find this information extremely valuable. We could also provide a service to a prospective user of a crowdfunding campaign, on ways that they can optimize their campaign itself to give themselves the best chance of being successful.","topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236934},{"name":"ashishakonnur/YouTube-trends-for-2017-2018---Intro-to-Python","owner":"ashishakonnur","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishakonnur/YouTube-trends-for-2017-2018---Intro-to-Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236935},{"name":"gage-langdon/webrtc-playground","owner":"gage-langdon","html_url":"https://github.com/gage-langdon/webrtc-playground","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236936},{"name":"Wolfecode/ChessMimic","owner":"Wolfecode","html_url":"https://github.com/Wolfecode/ChessMimic","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"Chess AI that can play in the style of a given player. Chess AI currently are either algorithm based, and play like engines or they are highly trained 3000+ rated neural nets that are better than the world's best players. The goal of this project is to create a chess AI that plays at the skill level and in the style of a certain player. For example it can be trained on Anatoly Karpov and would play positionally, or if it were trained on Mihail Tal it would be aggressive and sacrifice frequently.","topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236937},{"name":"Wolfecode/GuessTheElo","owner":"Wolfecode","html_url":"https://github.com/Wolfecode/GuessTheElo","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"Chess AI that can guess the elo rating of chess players based on just a PNG game. In the future, look at what elo is required to see a certain move for a player.","topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236938},{"name":"Wolfecode/SocialStock","owner":"Wolfecode","html_url":"https://github.com/Wolfecode/SocialStock","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"An app that lets you trade social media as a stock. Invest in new creators you think will do well. If they do better than expected, get rewarded.","topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236939},{"name":"kristopher-smith/hello-world","owner":"kristopher-smith","html_url":"https://github.com/kristopher-smith/hello-world","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"I read the directions this time...yay!!!","topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236940},{"name":"scottyhq/scratch","owner":"scottyhq","html_url":"https://github.com/scottyhq/scratch","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"Scratch space","topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236941},{"name":"thigmotaxis/git_test","owner":"thigmotaxis","html_url":"https://github.com/thigmotaxis/git_test","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236942},{"name":"shawnlee5482/react-hook","owner":"shawnlee5482","html_url":"https://github.com/shawnlee5482/react-hook","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1798.4,"global_rank":236943},{"name":"AlbertDavletov/architecture-sprint-6","owner":"AlbertDavletov","html_url":"https://github.com/Albert